      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Now that you have seen how all the constituent parts work, we can put them together to do something useful."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The execution of business services can sometimes fail due to concurrency issues (for example, a deadlock loser). If the operation is retried, it is likely to succeed on the next try. For business services where it is appropriate to retry in such conditions (idempotent operations that do not need to go back to the user for conflict resolution), we want to transparently retry the operation to avoid the client seeing a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "PessimisticLockingFailureException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This is a requirement that clearly cuts across multiple services in the service layer and, hence, is ideal for implementing through an aspect."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Because we want to retry the operation, we need to use around advice so that we can call "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "proceed"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " multiple times. The following listing shows the basic aspect implementation:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./ConcurrentOperationExecutor[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Around(\"com.xyz.CommonPointcuts.businessService()\")"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " references the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "businessService"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " named pointcut defined in "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Sharing Named Pointcut Definitions"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "core/aop/ataspectj/pointcuts.html#aop-common-pointcuts"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Note that the aspect implements the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Ordered"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " interface so that we can set the precedence of the aspect higher than the transaction advice (we want a fresh transaction each time we retry). The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "maxRetries"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "order"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " properties are both configured by Spring. The main action happens in the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "doConcurrentOperation"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " around advice. Notice that, for the moment, we apply the retry logic to each "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "businessService"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". We try to proceed, and if we fail with a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "PessimisticLockingFailureException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", we try again, unless we have exhausted all of our retry attempts."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The corresponding Spring configuration follows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./ApplicationConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To refine the aspect so that it retries only idempotent operations, we might define the following "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Idempotent"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./service/Idempotent[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "We can then use the annotation to annotate the implementation of service operations. The change to the aspect to retry only idempotent operations involves refining the pointcut expression so that only "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Idempotent"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " operations match, as follows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./service/SampleService[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "An AOP Example"
      }
    ]
  }
}
